    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Expats Pickup Planning</h1>
    <p>A tourist's pickup is a counter moment; an expat's pickup is the founding visit of a year-long arrangement, and planning it properly turns a machine handover into the start of a system. The resident's pickup happens at the shop's verified address at 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, during opening hours that run 09:00 to 21:00 daily, and the expat's planning job is to make that one visit do the work of ten: choosing well, inspecting together, asking everything, and leaving with the commute's first rehearsal already scheduled. This page builds that plan on verified facts only, with cautious guidance everywhere the shop's own answers belong, and no invented delivery or pickup arrangements.</p>
    <p>The page is part of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster, written for expats. The verified fleet prices sit on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, the general question bank is on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the paperwork questions that the pickup visit should ask are collected in this cluster's expat paperwork guide.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">The resident's pickup, rethought</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">Choosing the day and the hour</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">The route to the counter is the first commute</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">Arriving with the resident's question set</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">The machine walkaround, done together</a></li>
